// Every MCP tool's `run` (the tool table in `scene.j3` points here): arguments to scene requests, `check` and
// `play` through `driver.run`, render, import, asset search and fetch, gen.
//
// Port of: j3c/src/mcp/ops.rs, (mcp/server.rs `run_tool` arms)
// J3: Scene ops call `scene.ops.runTool` in-process (plan 11 B12.1), or the open editor through Rust's
// events/replies file protocol (B12.2 deferred). `play` and `check` build through `driver.run()` with a fresh
// `Session` (B12.6), not by spawning `j3c build`; only running the game stays a subprocess. Their answers carry
// the `Diag`s (code, severity, path, line, col, msg) as a `"diags"` member written last (B12.7).
// J3: `state` is `&mcp.server.State`. Every fn here is `Err("... not ported yet")` until the MCP chunk.
// J3: Deferred (user, 2026-11-18): not ported yet; stubs keep their signatures. See plans/12-deferred-tools.md.
module j3c.mcp.ops;

use j3.data.json.Json;
use j3.memory.Arena;
use j3.result.Result;
use j3c.mcp.schema.Answer;

